{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470162-ways-of-protecting-unique-instrument-wonder","id":1470162,"title":"Ways of protecting unique instrument/wonder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-10T13:39:55-08:00","id":1470162,"title":"Ways of protecting unique instrument/wonder","content":"I have this idea of having a wristwatch that is both an unique instrument and a wonder. Losing an unique instrument is almost as bad as dying. I find the &quot;cast without instruments&quot; rule for casting without unique instruments very harsh. Having to spend a WP point and +3 diff on Arete roll is absurd. So, I wonder if this unique thing is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the spheres my mage has are not very good to protect it (Forces, Life, Prime). No Matter and Prime is only 1. So how could I guarantee the watch will be safe? <br /> Being a wonder makes it harder to break?<br /> <br /> Also, the uniqueness of the watch relies on the fact that the mage love it and doesn't even like to be more than a few moments without it. He found his way into the watch, it wasn't given by any loving friend/parent/etc.<br /> Just as focus can change, familiars can be made, can am unique instrument be replaced by another on the long run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T14:46:56-08:00","id":1470166,"title":"","content":"To an extent, there's a conversation to be had with your ST, since how hard it will be to reclaim or replace a unique instrument is going to be on them.<br /> <br /> If it's not too late, the Phylactery Flaw would give you the points to buy some Correspondence, and makes retrieving the item exceedingly simple if its taken from you (though if it's destroyed it's even worse).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would advise against it given your stated preferences, concerns, and the justification. &quot;My favorite watch,&quot; doesn't explain why it's so important to your mage's magical working.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T20:52:11-08:00","id":1470187,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> If the wonder has a Correspondence effect, maybe I could make it tp back after some time away form the mage. FbdF has a quote about self activating wonders. I can't buy Correspondence. Also, I'm more concerned about it being destroyed. So, the fact that it is a wonder doesn't make it more resistant?<br /> <br /> You don't think the -1 diff in Arete roll is worth it?<br /> <br /> And the unique instrument must be always given by someone important to the mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T21:20:00-08:00","id":1470189,"title":"","content":"If you make it a Wonder, that's certainly a way to have it be harder to destroy, but Wonders aren't harder to destroy by default.<br /> <br /> Are you using Rev. or M20 rules here?<br /> <br /> And who gave it to the mage isn't as important compared to why it is both so important to the mage and how it factors into the mage's style. A watch might be really important to a mage, but to be a unique instrument it still needs to qualify as an instrument in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T21:44:41-08:00","id":1470190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> M20, but FbdF is more complete, so we use it as well.<br /> <br /> A watch can be an instrument. There are several entries that it ould fit. And why could it be so important to a mage to the point of being unique without someone giving to him? Ant ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T21:55:39-08:00","id":1470191,"title":"","content":"Why it's important is going to be a matter of magical style. Something the mage created or built themselves is pretty common for this IME.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T12:43:19-08:00","id":1470233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470162-ways-of-protecting-unique-instrument-wonder?p=1470191#post1470191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why it's important is going to be a matter of magical style. Something the mage created or built themselves is pretty common for this IME.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage couldn't have created this wonder, since he lacks the spheres. <br /> What you mean by matter of magical style?<br /> As I see, the unique instrument is something of great value for the mage for whatever reason, that doesn't need to be complex. I could see an object being unique to a mage simply because he find it pretty or cool. Like Gollum and his &quot;precious&quot;. Or I could do something similar to Harry Potter and their wands, where the instrument chooses the mage or something like that.<br /> <br /> About the protection, there is nothing that can be done without Matter, right?<br /> The wonder will probably have Time 4 triggers, maybe a trigger that creates a Forces protection field and invisibility around it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T13:03:40-08:00","id":1470235,"title":"","content":"A mage can make something that a mentor/etc. enchants into a Wonder.<br /> <br /> And what I mean as a matter of magical style is that the instrument still has to match the mage's style. Just because a watch is a valid option for an instrument doesn't meant every mage can use watches as instruments. If a watch doesn't fit your mage's magical practice, it's not going to be a unique instrument no matter how much it has deep meaning for them. Or, in other words, you don't have to make something a unique instrument (and thus the risks/rewards associated with it) just because your character cares about it personally. In the Harry Potter example, wands are part of the magical style. Potterverse wizards don't have to use one specific wand to use magic, but wands are a vital part of magical practice (not getting into the really dumb stuff added after the initial books); but there's a whole thing about matching the right wand to the right wizard/witch for the maximum resonance (not quite a unique instrument outside of very special cases like the Elder Wand).<br /> <br /> For protection? Well, not with your starting Spheres. The problem is that we're talking about Mage. If another mage realizes you have a unique instrument and wants to destroy it, there are a lot of ways they can go about it. Correspondence (I know) and Prime are the most generalist approaches. Which Prime you can consecrate an item to yourself, which makes it much easier to keep hold of it (no separating it from you by tossing you into the Umbra) and get it back with Correspondence. Entropy is another options here (you can make it harder to break, even if not as well as Matter can, and have more tricks for getting it back if taken by force or theft in the moment).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T09:44:53-08:00","id":1470283,"title":"","content":"The mage doesn't have the skill to build a watch. <br /> Maybe I could relate the wonder with the mage's avatar somehow. And that relation could end up by making it unique? What you think?<br /> <br /> What consecrate does besides changing the object form when the mage shapechange? What kind of bond is made? Could the mage know its location or conditions automatically?<br /> <br /> As I said, maybe I could cast a forcefield on the wonder and hang it with Time 4 to be released by voice command whenever the watch is missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T14:52:15-08:00","id":1470299,"title":"","content":"OK... serious question here: Do you really want this to be a unique instrument because... you can just not do that. It can just be a cool Wonder that your mage loves, but if something happens to it you're not looking at massive spell casting penalties.<br /> <br /> It's clear that your character is too far a long to rebuild to make more capable of protecting a unique instrument from most casual/in-the-moment interference.<br /> <br /> It feels like either you should just drop the unique instrument for this character, or talk to the ST because the worry about the penalties for losing it are making this all unfun, and making sure it has some plot immunity until your mage is more powerful and can better defend it would let you just make the character you want and confront obstacles attached to unique instruments when they're more capable of overcoming them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T16:08:45-08:00","id":1470306,"title":"","content":"@heavyarms I don't need it to be unique, but I would like for the mage to have a very special bond to the wonder other than being a loved instrument.<br /> And the -1 in Arete rolls is pretty good. I don't know other reliable and easy mean of getting this bonus. All others apply to some specific scenario, or take more time in casting, or requires a specific focus.<br /> <br /> About the consecration, it is really just the shapechanging thing? I thought that the bond would make the mage conscious of the item state and position all the time, like a familisr in D&amp;D. Afterall, it is like the object were the mage itself, no?<br /> <br /> Also, Forces fields can cover almost any kind of damage (physical, heat, electric, all energy tbf).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T16:28:13-08:00","id":1470308,"title":"","content":"The watch being a Periapt that has a big pool of quintessence lets you toss -1 to -3 at a spell, and the cost can be handled in downtime rather that in the heat of the moment.<br /> <br /> But that's not going to cover the &quot;bond&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> As far as &quot;bonds&quot; go:<br /> <br /> Yes, there's unique instrument or the Phylactery Flaw (and your phylactery is a unique instrument inherently).<br /> You could have an nontraditional familiar that's a watch with secret functions.<br /> If you can think of something, the watch could be part of a Legend (which increases your quintessence access and spending that for difficulty reductions).<br /> The Wonder could be a Talisman with a literal piece of your mage's soul in it (those are the ones that can cast independently of the mage); esp since a more powerful mage would have to do this for them, that connection can have some mechanical effects.<br /> Using Prime for Consecration and then incorporating the watch into Body of Light isn't as special but it still has some effects; but you're still going to need to increase your Spheres to maximize those.<br /> <br /> The thing about Forces for a shield:<br /> <br /> 1) Vulgar.<br /> 2) Only stops energy. It isn't going to do anything if your instrument gets dropped in a vat of acid. It isn't going to protect against Correspondence theft, Entropy decay, or Prime destruction spells.<br /> 3) Isn't selective without more Spheres involved (you're going to need to drop the shield or cast extra magic just to charge/wind the watch).<br /> 4) Countermagic can degrade or remove the shield, and the ease of it being obvious magic to Sleepers will also degrade it as well (or saddle you with Permadox or something similar).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T20:23:15-08:00","id":1470327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470162-ways-of-protecting-unique-instrument-wonder?p=1470308#post1470308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The watch being a Periapt that has a big pool of quintessence lets you toss -1 to -3 at a spell, and the cost can be handled in downtime rather that in the heat of the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talisman can hold quintessence. However the mage would have to constantly fill it. It's not an automstic bonus like the unique instrument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470162-ways-of-protecting-unique-instrument-wonder?p=1470308#post1470308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that's not going to cover the &amp;quot;bond&amp;quot; thing.<br /> <br /> As far as &amp;quot;bonds&amp;quot; go:<br /> <br /> Yes, there's unique instrument or the Phylactery Flaw (and your phylactery is a unique instrument inherently).<br /> You could have an nontraditional familiar that's a watch with secret functions.<br /> If you can think of something, the watch could be part of a Legend (which increases your quintessence access and spending that for difficulty reductions).<br /> The Wonder could be a Talisman with a literal piece of your mage's soul in it (those are the ones that can cast independently of the mage); esp since a more powerful mage would have to do this for them, that connection can have some mechanical effects.<br /> Using Prime for Consecration and then incorporating the watch into Body of Light isn't as special but it still has some effects; but you're still going to need to increase your Spheres to maximize those.</div> </div> </div> </div>-Phylacteries are more dangerous than the unique instrument. Without it the mage can use magick at all. The only benefit over unique instruments is that you won't die unless your phylactery is safe, but you can't do anything without s body.<br /> <br /> -I already have a familiar and it's not the watch. Also, the watch is a wonder. I don't know of it can be both. Nor I would like it to.<br /> <br /> - Legend background doesn't seems right for what I want<br /> <br /> - I'm not sure about the soul piece thing, but talismans can have some sort of automatism. That's something I'm thinking about too. Making the wonder cast an effect in case it is stolen or damaged...<br /> <br /> - Consecrating cam be done with any object with how many you want. The watch won't be special. Also, I already plan to consecrate it anyway.<br /> <br /> Do you think that an unique instrument is risky but a phylactery isn't???<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470162-ways-of-protecting-unique-instrument-wonder?p=1470308#post1470308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The thing about Forces for a shield:<br /> <br /> 1) Vulgar.<br /> 2) Only stops energy. It isn't going to do anything if your instrument gets dropped in a vat of acid. It isn't going to protect against Correspondence theft, Entropy decay, or Prime destruction spells.<br /> 3) Isn't selective without more Spheres involved (you're going to need to drop the shield or cast extra magic just to charge/wind the watch).<br /> 4) Countermagic can degrade or remove the shield, and the ease of it being obvious magic to Sleepers will also degrade it as well (or saddle you with Permadox or something similar).</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I must clarify that the plan is to activate the shield with a Time 4 trigger. So, it is not a always running shield.<br /> <br /> 1- Not worried about paradox if the wonder is in danger<br /> 2- Energy and physical damage. That includes physically breaking, fire/electricity/etc, and even the acif, since the field would repel everything from touching the wonder. I'm not sure about Prime and Entropy. Entropy would rust the wonder, amd the field would protect against everything (as if it was sealed in vacuum), so maybe only Prime could damage it.<br /> 3- Not if it's trigger activated<br /> 4- Countermagick is indeed a problem. But even if ade it indestructible with Matter one could counter magick it too.<br /> <br /> Now, in Book of Secrets page 301 we have this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Simple Charms or Trinkets should be easy to destroy, but powerful Talismans or Doomsday Machines ought to provide a dramatic sense of challenge and peril.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe this means high lvl wonders are harder to destroy? It would be a lvl 5 wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T19:45:25-08:00","id":1470405,"title":"","content":"I'll get right to the point.<br /> <br /> Unique Instrument doesn't have to be Unique in the literal sense. You must have an idea on how you recover/recreate it in the case it is destroyed.<br /> <br /> Now, if your watch is really irreplaceable and you can't explain how it fits your magic style, it clearly isn't fit for a Unique Instrument.<br /> <br /> And the -1 dif is good, but not that good. If you can't answer those questions easily (how it fits style, how to replace it), then it isn't worth the effort. You'll have a lot of other potential sources for dif reductions in practice, don't overthink this one. It is broad and risky by design.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that even if you were a Master in all Spheres, if a Mage decides they will destroy your watch no matter what, then it will probably be destroyed. So yeah, it should be replaceable somehow.<br /> <br /> Some examples of Unique Instruments:<br /> <br /> 1 - A wand made at exact specifications regarding wood, inlays of metal alloys, the time of construction and the tiny crystal in its end. The Mage believes the gestures and magic sigils must be made with a wand built under specifications derived from your Astral Map, if they lose the wand they'll have to calculate new specifications for it to be made in the next New Moon;<br /> <br /> 2 - For another anything will do... after a proper consecrating ritual. Their magic is enacted through the blessings of a Bishop enacted in a ceremony similar to the dedication of a church, and only one object may be so blessed and consecrated to them at a time. If or when the current one is lost, they'll have to atone for their sin and seek a Bishop with an entire morning of free time to enact the lengthy ritual;<br /> <br /> 3 - One works magic through infusions made with a plant watered with their own blood. They have a patch of those in their garden and a bag of dried leaves with themselves. If they lose those somehow, they'll have to procure the right seeds, find suitable land, and start the process of cultivation anew, no Instrument available until the first plants mature enough.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor an actually unique Instrument I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> that you're better with a Phylactery. It makes more sense and is better because you're actually refunded points for your trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T05:52:45-08:00","id":1470422,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> M20 doesn't say anything about replacing unique instrument, but I agree that it should be possible, since a mage can even change paradigm and practices.<br /> <br /> You have made very good points regarding the inevitable destruction of an instrument if one or more people are devoted to it. However, this might be true for the mage's life too, haha.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the thing with the watch, in a summarized explanation, is the singular mechanisms and crystals inside of it. The fluff of the mage is energy manipulation and the crystals inside the watch are very good amplifiers for it. The mechanisms inside it also help to control the energy as well as give the Talisman its powers.<br /> So, I guess that one way to replace it is to get it rebuilt with the same special crystals and characteristics as before, or somehow getting a new one with the exact characteristics.<br /> <br /> About the phylactery, I was considering it, but it is eay worse than the unique instrument, since you can't cast spells at all without it, while without the unique inst you can cast as if without tools.<br /> If the phylactery is destroyed you can't use magick for ever<br /> Phylacteries are not an instrument so they can't be dropped<br /> The only benefit of a phylactery is surviving if your body is destroyed, though you don't have a body so you can't do shit, and the 7 flaw point, which you can get elsewhere if needed.<br /> <br /> Now, about consecrating with Prime 1, what would be the benefits besides shapechanging and going to Umbra? And being a very weak spot for mages that get their hands on it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}